    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today leans heavily into the exploitable matchup against Aldegheri, vaulting both **Henry Bolte** (65.39) and **Max Muncy** (64.25) to the top of our daily projection board. **Henry Bolte** benefits from the rare \"perfect storm\" of a favorable park shift and a high-leadoff spot, while **Max Muncy** thrives due to the massive +19% boost derived from facing a sub-optimal opposing pitcher. **James Wood** (64.47) remains our most electric play of the day; despite a neutral platoon, his massive park factor (+16%) and aggressive base-running opportunity against Bradish make him a mandatory start in our pursuit of stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Alex Freeland** (47.81), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Kyle Karros** (55.11). While **Alex Freeland** offers a consistent floor, his eighth-spot placement in the order created a negative drag on his daily efficiency score compared to the positional flexibility and platoon advantage **Kyle Karros** holds against Prielipp. We are also keeping a close eye on **Corbin Carroll** (57.59); while his base projection is stellar, he faces a difficult matchup against Rasmussen, and his score is dampened by a negative park factor. If **Corbin Carroll** fails to utilize his elite sprint speed to disrupt the catcher, we will be relying on the high-floor performances of **Josh Naylor** (60.76) and **Austin Riley** (58.24) to maintain our category standings.\n\nWe must remain cautious with **Jose Caballero** (43.27). While he offers our best path to stolen base production, his poor lineup position and the elite skills of Gray, S present a significant risk of a sub-40 performance. With **Mickey Moniak** confirmed on the bench, our outfield depth is essentially tapped out; we are locked into this configuration, hoping that the favorable matchups for **Henry Bolte** and **Max Muncy** provide enough offensive cushion to offset the potential drag from our lower-scoring depth pieces like **Jose Caballero** and **Travis Bazzana**. We will continue to monitor the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Carson Williams** as we manage our long-term game caps.",
